WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.706 --> 00:00:17.576
The faint, reddish light from Zing's breath showed Zann that he and his friends were in a stone

2
00:00:17.636 --> 00:00:22.240
passageway. The place had a damp, dusty smell that tickled Zann's nose.

3
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.503
"Careful," Perda whispered as they started walking.

4
00:00:25.523 --> 00:00:28.506
"We don't know what could be hiding down here."

5
00:00:29.306 --> 00:00:31.068
Zann tried not to think about that.

6
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.864
He kept his gaze on Zing, who flew ahead, letting out an occasional burst of flame to light

7
00:00:36.884 --> 00:00:37.224
the way.

8
00:00:38.345 --> 00:00:40.906
Suddenly Zing spun around and leaped at him.

9
00:00:40.926 --> 00:00:43.048
"Whoa!" Zann cried.

10
00:00:43.068 --> 00:00:44.729
"What's the matter with you?

11
00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:47.251
This is no time for our game!"

12
00:00:47.991 --> 00:00:49.572
He tried to push the dragon aside.

13
00:00:50.513 --> 00:00:53.955
But Zing spat fire at him, narrowly missing Zann's arm.

14
00:00:54.956 --> 00:00:56.757
"Zing!" Zann scolded again.

15
00:00:56.777 --> 00:01:00.604
"Stop—" "Wait," Darb told Zann.

16
00:01:00.624 --> 00:01:02.385
"He might be trying to tell us something."

17
00:01:03.066 --> 00:01:04.367
Perda peered past them.

18
00:01:04.387 --> 00:01:06.228
"Look," she said.

19
00:01:06.248 --> 00:01:07.549
"There's a hole!"

20
00:01:08.349 --> 00:01:09.770
Zing relaxed and backed off.

21
00:01:10.531 --> 00:01:14.794
He scampered to the edge of the drop-off, blowing out a sheet of flame so they could see

22
00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:17.315
better. Zann gulped as he looked down.

23
00:01:18.056 --> 00:01:20.057
The hole was at least ten feet deep.

24
00:01:20.778 --> 00:01:22.499
And something at the bottom was moving.

25
00:01:22.519 --> 00:01:25.161
"What's down there?"

26
00:01:25.541 --> 00:01:26.842
Gliss sounded horrified.

27
00:01:26.862 --> 00:01:30.164
"It looks like a nest of cave hissers."

28
00:01:30.184 --> 00:01:30.784
Darb shuddered.

29
00:01:31.564 --> 00:01:35.165
"This must be a trap in case anyone tried to follow the king or queen."

30
00:01:35.866 --> 00:01:36.686
He patted Zing.

31
00:01:36.706 --> 00:01:38.446
"Thanks for the warning, little buddy."

32
00:01:39.127 --> 00:01:41.107
They picked their way carefully around the pit.

33
00:01:41.827 --> 00:01:43.368
After that nobody talked much.

34
00:01:44.068 --> 00:01:44.868
They just walked.

35
00:01:46.008 --> 00:01:46.709
And walked.

36
00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:49.309
And then walked some more.

37
00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:55.411
The tunnel took so many twists and turns that Zann completely lost his bearings.

38
00:01:56.171 --> 00:01:57.412
Then Zing stopped again.

39
00:01:57.432 --> 00:02:00.722
"Look! There's a fork in the tunnel," Darb said.

40
00:02:00.742 --> 00:02:02.784
"Which way should we go?"

41
00:02:03.244 --> 00:02:03.824
asked Perda.

42
00:02:03.844 --> 00:02:05.646
"Both tunnels go up."

43
00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:09.249
"Well, we have to take one of them," said Gliss.

44
00:02:09.269 --> 00:02:10.751
"I vote we go that way."

45
00:02:11.471 --> 00:02:13.213
Gliss pointed at the left-hand tunnel.

46
00:02:14.154 --> 00:02:16.355
They followed Zing's glowing breath up the tunnel.

47
00:02:18.057 --> 00:02:20.819
"Careful," Zann said as he stumbled over something.

48
00:02:20.839 --> 00:02:22.821
"There's a rock on the floor here."

49
00:02:23.582 --> 00:02:25.844
He waved the others past him so they wouldn't trip.

50
00:02:26.588 --> 00:02:29.470
Then he glanced down at the object on the floor.

51
00:02:30.251 --> 00:02:31.352
His eyes widened.

52
00:02:31.372 --> 00:02:34.354
"I was wrong, you guys," he said.

53
00:02:34.374 --> 00:02:35.715
"It's not a rock.

54
00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:37.236
It's a bone!"

55
00:02:38.156 --> 00:02:39.657
"What?" Gliss squeaked.

56
00:02:40.298 --> 00:02:41.399
"What kind of bone?"

57
00:02:42.559 --> 00:02:46.442
Suddenly a terrible howl echoed through the tunnel behind them.

58
00:02:47.203 --> 00:02:50.505
A huge, dark beast emerged right out of the wall!

59
00:02:50.525 --> 00:02:51.706
"Oh no!

60
00:02:52.166 --> 00:02:53.307
It's a shadow beast!"

61
00:02:53.627 --> 00:02:54.268
Darb shouted.

62
00:02:54.936 --> 00:02:55.536
"A what?"

63
00:02:55.876 --> 00:02:56.657
Perda exclaimed.

64
00:02:56.677 --> 00:02:58.977
"I didn't think they really existed."

65
00:02:59.237 --> 00:03:00.258
Darb sounded scared.

66
00:03:00.998 --> 00:03:02.479
"Run!" Zann yelled.

67
00:03:03.759 --> 00:03:07.280
They ran up the tunnel with the shadow beast chasing them.

68
00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:11.001
Perda was in the lead, but after a short distance, she skidded to a stop.

69
00:03:11.021 --> 00:03:12.322
"Dead end!"

70
00:03:12.782 --> 00:03:13.882
she cried breathlessly.

71
00:03:14.723 --> 00:03:16.183
Zann looked back, terrified.

72
00:03:16.903 --> 00:03:18.744
The monster was lurching right toward them!

73
00:03:19.468 --> 00:03:24.491
Just then Zing flew toward the beast, sending out a burst of flame and lighting up the whole

74
00:03:24.572 --> 00:03:28.995
tunnel. To everyone's amazement the shadow beast disappeared for a moment!

75
00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:30.936
"That's right!"

76
00:03:31.256 --> 00:03:31.736
Darb said.

77
00:03:31.756 --> 00:03:34.078
"Shadow beasts have to stay in the dark.

78
00:03:34.838 --> 00:03:36.019
The light destroys them."

79
00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:40.923
Zing continued to breathe fire while everyone quickly ran back down the tunnel.

80
00:03:41.523 --> 00:03:44.485
They reached the fork and dashed up the right-hand tunnel.

81
00:03:45.306 --> 00:03:46.386
Zing soon followed.

82
00:03:46.406 --> 00:03:49.480
"Whew, that was close," Perda said.

83
00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.902
"Yeah," Gliss said.

84
00:03:51.922 --> 00:03:54.144
"I hope this tunnel leads to the palace.

85
00:03:54.864 --> 00:03:57.626
Because I definitely don't want to pass that thing again!"

86
00:03:58.407 --> 00:03:59.227
Nobody answered.

87
00:03:59.848 --> 00:04:01.709
They all just started walking again.

88
00:04:02.449 --> 00:04:06.312
And soon they were climbing as the tunnel grew steeper and steeper.

89
00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:10.635
Just when Zann was starting to think they'd be climbing forever, Darb spoke.

90
00:04:10.655 --> 00:04:14.258
"Is it my imagination, or is it getting lighter in here?"

91
00:04:15.298 --> 00:04:17.220
Zann suddenly realized Darb was right.

92
00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:19.941
"There must be an opening nearby!"

93
00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:22.101
They hurried around the next corner.

94
00:04:22.781 --> 00:04:26.843
Just up ahead, pale light poured in through an opening at the end of the tunnel!

95
00:04:27.543 --> 00:04:34.165
The opening was large enough for a person to squeeze through—except it was completely crisscrossed with stout iron

96
00:04:34.225 --> 00:04:37.426
bars. "I think we found the palace!"

97
00:04:37.886 --> 00:04:38.626
Gliss exclaimed.

98
00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:42.187
Zann pressed his face against the iron bars.

99
00:04:42.827 --> 00:04:45.628
The opening was located near the floor of a large room.

100
00:04:46.376 --> 00:04:50.059
A pair of golden chairs stood in the center of the polished floor.

101
00:04:50.079 --> 00:04:52.641
"This must be the throne room!"

102
00:04:53.042 --> 00:04:53.662
Zann whispered.

103
00:04:53.682 --> 00:04:56.104
"Then where is everybody?"

104
00:04:56.405 --> 00:04:57.065
Perda murmured.

105
00:04:57.786 --> 00:04:58.506
Zann shrugged.

106
00:04:58.526 --> 00:05:02.830
"I'm sure the king and queen don't spend all their time here," he said.

107
00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:09.336
"All we have to do is wait for—" The crash of doors flying open drowned out the rest

108
00:05:09.376 --> 00:05:09.996
of his words.

109
00:05:10.757 --> 00:05:14.260
About a dozen people rushed into the throne room, talking loudly.

110
00:05:15.088 --> 00:05:18.850
Zann couldn't follow most of what they were saying, but they sounded upset.

111
00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:20.831
"Isn't that the queen?"

112
00:05:21.471 --> 00:05:24.772
Perda pointed to a statuesque woman with bright red hair.

113
00:05:25.833 --> 00:05:26.493
Zann nodded.

114
00:05:26.513 --> 00:05:27.954
"I see the king too.

115
00:05:28.814 --> 00:05:30.175
Let's try to get their attention."

116
00:05:30.835 --> 00:05:33.576
Before he could yell, there was a blinding flash of light.

117
00:05:34.356 --> 00:05:36.797
Zann had to squeeze his eyes shut for a second.

118
00:05:37.518 --> 00:05:39.779
When he opened them, the scene had changed.

119
00:05:40.699 --> 00:05:46.819
Morb was in the throne room, along with a dozen trolls and at least fifty tiny, stinging dragons!

120
00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:49.702
"No!" someone screamed.

121
00:05:49.722 --> 00:05:52.664
"Your Majesties—" "Get back!"

122
00:05:53.145 --> 00:05:54.846
the king's deep voice roared.

123
00:05:55.607 --> 00:05:59.630
Others were also shouting, screaming, or calling out various spells.

124
00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.713
Above the din Zann could hear Morb's chilling laugh.

125
00:06:04.514 --> 00:06:05.775
There was another flash of light.

126
00:06:06.535 --> 00:06:08.637
Thick, choking smoke filled the room.

127
00:06:09.618 --> 00:06:11.980
When it cleared, the scene had changed again.

128
00:06:13.024 --> 00:06:17.128
The king and queen were gone, along with the few other Reds who had been present.

129
00:06:17.848 --> 00:06:19.670
The trolls and dragons were gone too.

130
00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:22.912
Everyone else was frozen or unconscious.

131
00:06:23.773 --> 00:06:25.154
Morb had also vanished.

132
00:06:25.835 --> 00:06:29.518
But Zann could still hear the fading echo of his terrible cackle.
